WEBVTT

00:05.880 --> 00:07.960
The next designated area is E2.

00:08.470 --> 00:10.890
The shortest route would 
be over the mountain.

00:11.430 --> 00:13.510
Going around it would be safer.

00:13.510 --> 00:16.240
I'd prefer to go over the mountain.

00:17.020 --> 00:19.640
Everyone else will go around,

00:19.640 --> 00:22.750
so it's an appropriate time 
to try for first place.

00:24.370 --> 00:29.630
Very well. If your mind is set on it, 
I'll accompany you over the mountain.

00:29.630 --> 00:31.290
I appreciate that.

00:42.560 --> 00:48.360
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

01:52.440 --> 01:58.990
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:05.030 --> 02:06.600
Ayanokoji-senpai.

02:07.060 --> 02:09.470
<b>#12 After Vengeance</b>

02:07.480 --> 02:09.550
I have a question to ask you.

02:09.980 --> 02:11.220
Since this morning...

02:11.980 --> 02:15.240
No, since you first asked to accompany me,

02:15.240 --> 02:17.510
you've seemed to be 
thinking something over.

02:17.740 --> 02:19.610
Was it that evident?

02:21.240 --> 02:23.160
Allow me to apologize first.

02:24.240 --> 02:28.980
You won't be reaching the 
next designated area today.

02:30.670 --> 02:35.880
The reason I asked to go over the 
mountain was to lead you to this place.

02:35.880 --> 02:39.380
You've made a lot of 
friends at this school,

02:39.380 --> 02:41.880
formed many alliances,

02:41.880 --> 02:46.640
and slowly but surely begun 
showing your true ability.

02:46.960 --> 02:52.020
But, Ayanokoji-senpai, 
you don't belong at this school.

02:52.020 --> 02:54.900
I suppose I should ask why you think that.

02:54.900 --> 02:56.050
Because...

02:56.590 --> 02:59.770
you are from the White Room.

03:00.450 --> 03:02.690
As you may have intuited,

03:03.030 --> 03:07.230
I came to this school on 
Acting Chairman Tsukishiro's orders.

03:08.050 --> 03:09.690
Those orders...

03:10.230 --> 03:13.070
were to get you expelled.

03:13.540 --> 03:18.260
I'm going to injure you now 
and activate your alarm.

03:18.260 --> 03:21.980
The teachers will arrive 
and order you to drop out.

03:21.980 --> 03:23.050
Then you'll be expelled.

03:23.050 --> 03:28.460
You think if I lose here, I'm expelled?

03:29.220 --> 03:33.970
Then I'm afraid there's 
only one action I can take.

03:34.830 --> 03:40.190
Any violence inflicted on me will 
get us both expelled for fighting.

03:40.670 --> 03:41.950
Perhaps.

03:44.400 --> 03:44.950
Let us begin.

03:48.920 --> 03:50.700
That's one hit.

03:50.700 --> 03:53.690
Are you tired or hesitating?

03:54.220 --> 03:56.960
You should be capable of more than this.

03:57.240 --> 04:01.080
You think you can defeat 
me without fighting back?

04:03.690 --> 04:05.010
That's two.

04:05.410 --> 04:08.680
If that had landed, 
it would have ended the fight.

04:08.680 --> 04:11.180
You may act as confident as you like,

04:11.530 --> 04:14.060
but you cannot win if 
you don't fight back.

04:14.060 --> 04:16.920
But it's not like I can 
win if I <i>do</i> fight back.

04:16.920 --> 04:18.120
True.

04:18.690 --> 04:20.610
What will you do, then?

04:20.610 --> 04:22.170
I'm thinking that over.

04:22.170 --> 04:26.000
I hope you find the answer while 
you're still capable of standing.

04:28.770 --> 04:32.290
As you're already aware, 
that's hit number three.

04:32.290 --> 04:35.790
You are as skilled as the rumors say.

04:38.540 --> 04:40.830
I've realized what you're after.

04:41.600 --> 04:45.300
You want to break me without 
harming me physically.

04:45.980 --> 04:50.310
It does seem that I can't beat 
you with standard fighting.

04:51.100 --> 04:54.310
This me cannot.

04:59.570 --> 05:02.550
But the other me will defeat you here.

05:04.380 --> 05:06.110
And who might you be?

05:06.380 --> 05:11.860
I came back here from that 
place in order to stop you.

05:11.860 --> 05:13.030
"That place"?

05:13.410 --> 05:15.370
A dark place.

05:16.150 --> 05:17.820
I'm back from there.

05:18.880 --> 05:20.940
I don't blame you for not knowing me.

05:20.940 --> 05:24.510
We've never met face to face.

05:25.170 --> 05:27.220
I am not Nanase.

05:27.220 --> 05:29.350
The person standing before you now...

05:30.170 --> 05:32.100
is Matsuo Eiichiro.

05:32.570 --> 05:34.850
Matsuo Eiichiro?

05:35.310 --> 05:38.980
The son of the man your father killed.

05:39.400 --> 05:41.580
I'm merely borrowing this body.

05:41.580 --> 05:45.490
I stand here now to beat you.

05:46.120 --> 05:49.620
Borrowing that body? 
That's an amusing joke.

05:49.840 --> 05:53.070
I came here to destroy you.

05:53.870 --> 05:55.000
That's all!

06:07.260 --> 06:10.930
I swear... I swear I will beat you!

06:11.760 --> 06:13.010
I will!

06:14.010 --> 06:15.820
You must pay the price!

06:23.520 --> 06:26.330
I understand what you're after.

06:26.710 --> 06:30.680
Nanase, you don't have 
multiple personalities,

06:30.680 --> 06:33.410
and you're not possessed 
by anyone's spirit.

06:33.410 --> 06:34.610
Then...

06:35.120 --> 06:37.750
Then how do you explain 
the fact that I'm here?!

06:38.310 --> 06:43.990
You've just forced the creation 
of another personality inside you.

06:44.660 --> 06:49.260
The differences in your speech and 
deportment come from autosuggestion.

06:49.260 --> 06:53.640
What I can do is the 
proof that I am who I am!

06:54.120 --> 06:59.640
Mere fluctuations within the range of 
what you've always been capable of.

06:59.640 --> 07:01.300
Y-You're wrong!

07:01.680 --> 07:04.900
I... I am Matsuo!

07:04.900 --> 07:09.650
If that were true, my words wouldn't 
be getting to you like this.

07:10.650 --> 07:13.260
You've just changed into a more 
combative version of yourself

07:13.260 --> 07:16.000
through the use of 
"other self" as a keyword.

07:16.000 --> 07:16.790
No!

07:16.790 --> 07:19.980
You want to believe that Matsuo's 
ghost has possessed you.

07:20.540 --> 07:23.920
I don't think you even believe it.

07:23.920 --> 07:26.690
Why... Why?

07:27.250 --> 07:28.920
I almost had you.

07:29.500 --> 07:31.050
I almost had you!

07:31.050 --> 07:33.490
You aren't nearly strong enough.

07:33.490 --> 07:37.810
We could do this until you die, 
and you would never land a hit.

07:38.500 --> 07:41.660
If you really want to get me expelled,

07:41.660 --> 07:44.940
the best way would be 
to pretend to be a victim.

07:45.160 --> 07:49.370
Rumple up your clothes a little 
and I'll have no recourse.

07:51.070 --> 07:52.090
I...

07:52.780 --> 07:53.830
I...

08:05.490 --> 08:09.260
Hey, you know that transceiver 
message you sent me this morning?

08:09.260 --> 08:13.180
I'd love to hear more 
about that, Yagami-kun.

08:13.640 --> 08:18.110
Nanase-san is joined to 
Ayanokoji-senpai at the hip.

08:18.740 --> 08:21.980
Nanase? That girl from Class 1-D?

08:21.980 --> 08:27.050
Nanase-san wants to drag 
Ayanokoji-senpai into a fight,

08:27.050 --> 08:29.360
and get him expelled for fighting back.

08:29.580 --> 08:34.850
So Nanase's going to report to the 
school that Ayanokoji beat her up?

08:35.310 --> 08:39.910
We're supposed to get some 
footage of it on a tablet.

08:39.910 --> 08:44.500
I'd like you to handle the recording.

08:44.500 --> 08:47.360
Huh? Why should I?

08:47.360 --> 08:49.250
Just do it yourself.

08:49.250 --> 08:51.260
I'm a guy.

08:51.260 --> 08:56.010
People might wonder why 
I saw it and didn't intervene.

08:56.370 --> 08:59.230
But you're a delicate young lady.

08:59.230 --> 09:01.230
You can say you were too scared to act,

09:01.230 --> 09:04.920
but recorded it on your tablet 
to at least get evidence.

09:06.450 --> 09:09.150
You'll do it, won't you, Kushida-senpai?

09:09.660 --> 09:11.490
Do I even have a choice?

09:15.080 --> 09:18.100
<i>They seem to have stopped.</i>

09:18.660 --> 09:21.440
<i>Proceed northwest slowly.</i>

09:22.160 --> 09:24.070
<i>Don't forget to record.</i>

09:27.460 --> 09:29.440
Not a sound, if you please.

09:29.780 --> 09:35.050
You don't want Ayanokoji-senpai and 
Nanase-chan to know you're here, do you,

09:35.050 --> 09:37.310
Kushida-senpai?

09:41.610 --> 09:42.970
So, um...

09:42.970 --> 09:46.100
What brings you here, Amasawa-san?

09:46.100 --> 09:51.330
I happened to be passing by 
when I saw you sneaking around.

09:51.330 --> 09:53.480
I wasn't sneaking!

09:53.480 --> 09:54.680
I was just...

09:54.680 --> 09:58.450
Right, I was taking a 
little walk, I suppose!

10:01.950 --> 10:03.450
Wh-What?!

10:03.690 --> 10:08.460
Coming this far into the mountains 
alone, sniffing around...

10:08.460 --> 10:10.580
What could you be after, I wonder?

10:10.580 --> 10:12.690
Wh-What do you mean?

10:13.230 --> 10:16.210
Amasawa-san, what are you accusing me of?!

10:16.210 --> 10:19.720
How long can you keep 
that mask from slipping?

10:20.160 --> 10:21.950
Can't wait to find out.

10:21.950 --> 10:23.350
S-Stay back!

10:23.620 --> 10:25.310
Nope!

10:28.140 --> 10:31.650
D-Do you realize what you're doing?

10:31.650 --> 10:34.900
Oh, I'm being practically 
gentle right now.

10:34.900 --> 10:38.060
No pain, now. No pain.

10:38.060 --> 10:40.490
Why are you doing this? 
I don't understand!

10:40.710 --> 10:42.190
Oh, really?

10:42.190 --> 10:46.830
Maybe using a closed fist 
will make my meaning clear!

10:49.910 --> 10:51.360
I-I'm sorry.

10:51.360 --> 10:54.750
Y-You just lashed out so suddenly, I...

10:54.750 --> 10:57.100
Still playing the meek little thing?

10:57.100 --> 11:01.130
Kushida-senpai, I know all about you.

11:01.130 --> 11:06.350
An ugly little monster convinced 
beyond a doubt that she's beautiful.

11:06.350 --> 11:10.540
Wanna cry to the school 
about how I hit you?

11:10.540 --> 11:14.620
You'd have a chance of 
getting me expelled...

11:14.620 --> 11:17.610
But I won't go without a fight.

11:17.610 --> 11:20.210
I'll reveal the dark secret 
from your middle school days

11:20.210 --> 11:21.430
you've worked so hard to hide,

11:21.430 --> 11:24.620
and make this a place 
you can't stay at all.

11:24.620 --> 11:25.790
How did you...

11:26.940 --> 11:29.140
"How did you know about my secret?"

11:29.140 --> 11:31.670
"Did Ayanokoji-senpai tell you?"

11:31.670 --> 11:35.170
I assume that's what you're 
thinking, but nope.

11:35.170 --> 11:38.110
As it happens, I'm special.

11:38.110 --> 11:40.690
Nothing escapes my watchful gaze.

11:40.690 --> 11:42.480
The hell is your problem?

11:42.480 --> 11:44.930
Just who even are you?!

11:44.930 --> 11:47.160
I'm simply...

11:48.310 --> 11:51.500
someone who came here 
to save Ayanokoji-senpai.

11:51.500 --> 11:52.450
What?

11:52.880 --> 11:58.160
I don't know who asked you to 
do this, but you're being used.

11:58.160 --> 11:59.970
You're a total novice at tailing people.

11:59.970 --> 12:03.430
Ayanokoji-senpai would 
obviously know you're here.

12:04.220 --> 12:06.200
What do you care about it?!

12:06.200 --> 12:08.530
Oh, I care <i>very</i> much.

12:08.530 --> 12:13.710
Because Ayanokoji-senpai 
is very special to me.

12:13.710 --> 12:17.840
Huh? What's this crap? 
You like him or something?

12:17.840 --> 12:21.350
Could you not trivialize my 
feelings with such vulgar words?

12:21.670 --> 12:24.300
I don't like him. I <i>love</i> him.

12:25.550 --> 12:29.640
Or maybe it's something 
even more powerful.

12:29.640 --> 12:33.130
A feeling that far exceeds love!

12:33.130 --> 12:34.880
That's why I care.

12:35.230 --> 12:38.280
So it's down the mountain 
and back to camp for you.

12:40.060 --> 12:41.900
Screw that.

12:42.990 --> 12:46.660
I'll get something on Ayanokoji and 
have him expelled no matter what!

12:46.660 --> 12:52.120
I can't let an outsider like you do that.

12:52.120 --> 12:54.050
L-Let me go!

12:54.050 --> 12:55.750
I don't think I will.

12:55.750 --> 12:58.980
You're insane.

12:59.900 --> 13:05.030
"I'm always the prettiest. 
I'm always the best."

13:05.030 --> 13:10.760
You really are in love with yourself, 
aren't you, Kushida-senpai?

13:11.130 --> 13:16.440
You're in such a frenzy to learn people's 
secrets, to have something on them.

13:16.440 --> 13:20.520
And by the same token, you hate it 
when people get something on you.

13:20.520 --> 13:24.500
"Anyone who learns my secret must pay."

13:24.500 --> 13:28.490
You're so extra. I kind of like it.

13:28.740 --> 13:31.510
I'm not going to lose.

13:31.510 --> 13:34.420
No matter what happens, 
I'll never give up.

13:35.290 --> 13:38.880
But here you are now, totally at my mercy.

13:38.880 --> 13:41.160
I'm in no rush.

13:41.530 --> 13:43.630
I just need to get rid of you, too.

13:43.970 --> 13:46.370
To get rid of anyone in my way—

13:46.370 --> 13:48.490
That's all I need to do.

13:48.490 --> 13:50.760
You're even better than I imagined.

13:50.760 --> 13:53.530
You're a dirty little bitch,

13:53.530 --> 13:56.510
but you've got an iron will 
that I can't help but admire.

13:57.050 --> 14:01.650
Instead of getting scared, 
you're overflowing with hatred.

14:01.650 --> 14:07.740
Not just for me... but for 
whoever spilled your secret.

14:07.740 --> 14:08.990
I wouldn't try it.

14:08.990 --> 14:12.770
You'll never put one over 
on me in a million years.

14:12.770 --> 14:13.990
Bye-bye.

14:18.330 --> 14:21.190
This really is an awful match-up for you.

14:21.190 --> 14:24.690
I don't have any secrets 
you can hold over my head.

14:24.690 --> 14:28.090
And with regard to Ayanokoji-senpai...

14:28.090 --> 14:34.500
I think you'll find getting him 
expelled just as hard as beating me.

14:34.500 --> 14:35.350
'Kay?

14:36.270 --> 14:40.090
Well, see ya! I gotta go 
see Ayanokoji-senpai.

14:40.090 --> 14:42.220
Will you tell him about me?

14:42.220 --> 14:43.880
Naw, no way!

14:44.820 --> 14:50.670
But you may still get what you're after.

14:51.330 --> 14:55.370
Ayanokoji-senpai could end up expelled.

14:56.040 --> 14:59.540
Then I'll crush you after that.

14:59.540 --> 15:02.820
Because I <i>will</i> crush you.

15:02.820 --> 15:04.750
Oh, Kushida-senpai.

15:04.750 --> 15:07.780
That fight was over before it began.

15:13.690 --> 15:17.240
What the hell am I doing?

15:27.080 --> 15:29.050
So it's broken?

15:29.050 --> 15:33.070
Yeah. I think it happened when 
I tripped and hit it on the rock.

15:33.380 --> 15:37.130
But it might be a little dangerous 
to go make the swap yourself.

15:37.130 --> 15:39.200
The weather's getting bad, too.

15:39.200 --> 15:41.220
I realize it's dangerous.

15:41.220 --> 15:43.420
But we can't afford to lose a single point

15:43.420 --> 15:45.740
if we want to catch up with the leaders.

15:46.340 --> 15:52.140
I'm sorry to do it after we increased 
our group size and met up, though.

15:52.140 --> 15:55.380
Well, if your watch isn't working, 
you don't have a choice.

15:55.380 --> 15:57.350
Just don't push yourself too hard, okay?

15:57.350 --> 16:01.460
Sure. I don't want to get 
hurt and drop out, either.

16:03.530 --> 16:06.740
What in the world am I doing?

16:07.190 --> 16:10.010
It's like I can't do anything right.

16:10.010 --> 16:13.970
The teachers seem to be watching us.

16:14.410 --> 16:17.450
Mashima, in particular, 
seems extremely alert.

16:17.450 --> 16:20.200
<i>The acting chairman and Shiba-sensei?</i>

16:20.430 --> 16:25.420
And Class 2-D's teacher, Chabashira, 
has been looking into our histories.

16:25.770 --> 16:28.950
Chabashira-sensei and Mashima-sensei...

16:29.280 --> 16:33.350
They're both in touch with 
Ayanokoji-kun, aren't they?

16:34.010 --> 16:38.850
I altered the records myself, 
so they shouldn't find anything there.

16:39.160 --> 16:40.860
Much appreciated.

16:40.860 --> 16:46.040
But as long as there's a chance 
he could find a foothold,

16:46.040 --> 16:49.370
we must find a way to remove him.

16:49.680 --> 16:53.620
But will he be that easy to expel?

16:53.950 --> 16:55.220
He came from the White Room—

16:55.220 --> 16:58.620
People are always led 
astray by those titles.

16:58.910 --> 17:00.450
<i>White Room?</i>

17:00.450 --> 17:07.750
If he survives to the last day, 
we'll bury him in Area I2 as planned.

17:19.220 --> 17:24.730
You're Ichinose Honami 
of Class 2-C, aren't you?

17:26.000 --> 17:29.830
It doesn't matter to me 
how much you heard.

17:30.230 --> 17:33.410
I need to get rid of you immediately.

17:35.030 --> 17:38.830
You're surely being hasty, Shiba-sensei.

17:39.180 --> 17:41.110
Yes, pardon me.

17:41.490 --> 17:44.370
I-I didn't hear anything.

17:44.980 --> 17:50.100
Being an adult means always 
preparing for the worst.

17:50.540 --> 17:58.130
I'm afraid I must proceed as 
though you heard everything.

17:58.780 --> 18:05.520
If what we said here gets out, 
we will end up in very big trouble.

18:05.880 --> 18:10.960
Perhaps we should torture you until 
you lose your memory and drop out?

18:13.650 --> 18:14.890
Just kidding.

18:15.250 --> 18:17.020
As a defender of this school,

18:17.020 --> 18:20.000
that's the kind of thing I must never say.

18:20.430 --> 18:24.790
I would like to avoid violence 
under any circumstances.

18:25.770 --> 18:27.970
Thus, I have a suggestion.

18:27.970 --> 18:30.380
If you tell anyone about this,

18:30.380 --> 18:36.520
I will force one group of 
Class 2-C's students to drop out.

18:38.220 --> 18:45.060
Of course, it will be a group without 
enough private points to avoid expulsion.

18:45.060 --> 18:48.020
The harbor is just ahead.

18:48.610 --> 18:49.710
Please go there.

18:59.060 --> 19:04.980
Don't forget. The ones you should 
protect are your classmates.

19:08.430 --> 19:12.610
Would you please tell me 
why you came after me?

19:13.090 --> 19:17.800
I wanted to avenge Matsuo Eiichiro.

19:18.120 --> 19:20.490
That's why I came to this school.

19:21.330 --> 19:23.770
From kindergarten to middle school,

19:24.160 --> 19:28.570
I was always with Eiichiro-kun, 
who was one year older.

19:30.450 --> 19:33.460
He was better than me in everything.

19:33.790 --> 19:35.950
He was my role model.

19:36.500 --> 19:43.590
But his father was the one who arranged 
for you to escape from the White Room,

19:43.990 --> 19:47.020
and the two of them lost 
everything they held dear.

19:48.430 --> 19:53.260
Even after losing a chance at an 
education, even after losing his father...

19:53.260 --> 19:56.460
Eiichiro-kun was always 
optimistic and smiling.

19:56.460 --> 19:58.970
He said he'd never give up.

19:59.760 --> 20:01.350
"If you can't see them again,

20:01.350 --> 20:03.760
you'll never get to
tell them how you feel."

20:04.320 --> 20:06.000
That's what you said.

20:06.000 --> 20:10.110
And that's when he came to me.

20:10.420 --> 20:12.100
Tsukishiro?

20:12.600 --> 20:15.930
He told me what destroyed 
Eiichiro-kun's life,

20:16.430 --> 20:18.490
and arranged for me to come to the school.

20:19.610 --> 20:22.780
He promised that if I 
could have you expelled,

20:22.780 --> 20:26.490
he'd arrange for me to meet your father.

20:27.010 --> 20:29.240
You haven't done anything wrong.

20:29.550 --> 20:36.940
But... I needed someone to take 
my anger and resentment out on.

20:38.290 --> 20:41.530
Since I couldn't carry out 
the acting chairman's orders,

20:42.140 --> 20:44.510
there's no point in me staying here.

20:45.310 --> 20:47.720
You'll leave the school?

20:47.720 --> 20:52.480
It's the closest thing 
I can do to atonement.

20:55.320 --> 20:57.210
You have nothing to be ashamed of.

20:57.790 --> 21:01.430
You used everything at your 
disposal to try to avenge him.

21:03.780 --> 21:06.240
But there's a reason 
I can't let you beat me.

21:06.910 --> 21:09.840
I think my remaining at this school

21:09.840 --> 21:12.690
is the only way to strike 
back at that man...

21:12.690 --> 21:15.870
at my father.

21:16.150 --> 21:21.380
It's selfish, but I would like to ask 
you to remain here and help me.

21:21.680 --> 21:24.540
If Tsukishiro has me expelled,

21:24.540 --> 21:29.390
it would be abandoning Matsuo, 
who helped me escape.

21:29.390 --> 21:35.270
So I had it all backwards, then?

21:37.540 --> 21:39.400
Will you help me?

21:40.120 --> 21:41.520
I promise I will.

21:44.410 --> 21:47.220
<i>That man and I are the same at the core.</i>

21:47.870 --> 21:49.790
<i>But we differ in other ways.</i>

21:50.780 --> 21:56.040
<i>He would never offer a helping 
hand to a useless fool.</i>

21:56.420 --> 21:59.390
<i>It doesn't matter if she's 
really useful or not.</i>

22:00.010 --> 22:02.420
<i>What's essential is to get</i>

22:02.980 --> 22:06.540
<i>what use you can out of them, 
even if it's as a sacrificial pawn.</i>
